-- The launcher this project builds with, and the only file `eliotw` reads. Keeping it out of
-- `eliot.pkg` is what lets the wrapper stay a dumb script: a shell loop over lines is not a parser,
-- and the wrapper has to work in a checkout that no eliot has ever run in.
--
-- The hash is not typed by hand. Bump the version to a bare tag, run the wrapper once, and it
-- records the hash of what it fetched from the canonical source — never from a mirror, since what a
-- committed hash is for is that a redirected download cannot substitute past it.
